  "Question": "The sum of two prime numbers is \\(85.\\) What is the product of these two prime numbers?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( 85 \\)",
    "B": "\\( 91 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 115 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 133 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 166 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Two odd numbers have an even sum. Since \\(85\\) is odd, one of the two primes must be even. The only even prime is \\(2\\), because every larger even number has \\(2\\) as a factor besides \\(1\\) and itself.\n\nThe other prime must therefore be \\(85-2=83\\), so their product is\n\\[\n2\\times83=166.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(166\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
